   "l": "Laws and edicts the more conspicuous —\nand thieves and robbers, many there are.",
   "v": true,
   "i": "The more the statutes are made plain, the more thieves and robbers there are.",
   "n": "彰 is 'made to stand out' — publication, the law posted up where all can read it. The claim is not that law breeds theft by magic: a sharper line drawn between what is mine and what is yours makes more things stealable, and gives the name 'thief' to more men. Chapter 19 said it from the other end — 絕巧棄利，盜賊無有.\n\n多有 puts the quantity first and the existence second: 'many — there are'."
